    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d798">

                <pb facs="0903" n="818" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg818"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">867.48/1119</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Counselor of the British Embassy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Barclay</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Assistant Secretary of State</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Phillips</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1918-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19,
                        1918</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1396</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Dear Mr. Phillips</hi>: On December 10th Mr.
                        Chilton<anchor n="12" xml:id="d798-f1"/> handed to Mr. Jones<anchor n="13"
                        xml:id="d798-f2"/> a copy of a telegram from His Majesty’s Representative at
                    Constantinople to the Foreign Office dated December 5th embodying a message from
                    Dr. Gates to the Department of State.<anchor n="14" xml:id="d798-f3"/> I have
                    now received a further telegram from Constantinople through the Foreign Office
                    stating that Dr. Gates asks that the following may be transmitted to the State
                    Department: <pb facs="0904" n="819" xml:id="pg819"/>
                    <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“When will the Belief Expedition fitting out for Turkey sail? Greatest
                            need of haste.</p>
                        <p>“Conditions here are becoming desperate. Turkish currency much
                            depreciated. Expedition should bring gold and as much coal as
                            possible.”</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>Believe me [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colville Barclay</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
